# WARP / corporate-MITM CA bundles. The agent's Dockerfile picks up any
# `.crt` file under `apps/agent/ca/` and trusts it inside the build, so
# `curl`/`npm install` steps can reach external HTTPS through a
# Cloudflare WARP-style decrypting proxy. Drop the host bundle (e.g.
# `/usr/local/share/ca-certificates/extra-ca.crt`) at
# `apps/agent/ca/warp-ca.crt` locally; not committed because it's
# host-specific. The `apps/agent/ca/` directory itself is tracked via
# its `.keep` so the Dockerfile's COPY always has a source.
apps/agent/ca/*.crt


node_modules/
.wrangler/
*.sqlite
*.sqlite-wal
*.sqlite-shm
.screenshots/

